WEBVTT

00:01.793 --> 00:03.545
This is interesting.

00:03.628 --> 00:06.214
How did you get here?

00:07.132 --> 00:09.884
The guards didn’t fire a single shot,

00:09.968 --> 00:13.388
which means you infiltrated
without a fight.

00:17.475 --> 00:19.310
By air? No…

00:21.354 --> 00:22.814
Through a tunnel?

00:22.897 --> 00:25.692
That is truly elegant!

00:27.569 --> 00:32.490
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA "JUMP COMICS"

02:11.798 --> 02:14.134
These are the stables inside the fortress.

02:14.217 --> 02:16.553
Damn, why did we come out here
of all places?

02:16.636 --> 02:18.221
It was just a miscalculation.

02:19.180 --> 02:21.224
It was factored in to some extent.

02:23.643 --> 02:26.020
Please, be quiet.

02:29.107 --> 02:31.651
Suika! Are you okay?

02:33.027 --> 02:34.445
These…

02:36.990 --> 02:39.909
These are all Yellow Dent corn kernels.

02:41.744 --> 02:46.166
If we grew as much corn
as Dr. Xeno has stacked,

02:46.249 --> 02:49.085
we could make as many meals
and Revival Fluid as we wanted.

02:49.168 --> 02:52.422
It feels like we could bring
all of humanity back to life!

03:08.229 --> 03:10.732
What is this? A watermelon?

03:25.830 --> 03:27.957
-What's wrong?
-Ouch…

03:28.041 --> 03:30.335
Suddenly, my stomach feels upset!

03:30.418 --> 03:34.172
Could I ask Dr. Xeno for some medicine?

03:35.506 --> 03:37.675
Hey! Don't puke here, you idiot!

03:38.426 --> 03:39.886
A lot came up…

04:13.628 --> 04:17.590
Awesome!
This is real 21st-century science!

04:18.925 --> 04:22.262
-You…
-No way, did we get caught already?

04:23.805 --> 04:25.098
We can't stay any longer.

04:33.273 --> 04:34.357
Hurry!

04:35.817 --> 04:38.945
They're coming!
The enemies are getting closer!

04:39.028 --> 04:40.363
Don't worry about it!

04:41.364 --> 04:43.616
I'll blow everything up all at once
with this bomb!

04:44.575 --> 04:47.620
<i>With the explosion,</i>
<i>the basket carrying Xeno goes "Whoosh!"</i>

04:47.704 --> 04:49.580
<i>as it escapes</i>
<i>and blocks the castle entrance.</i>

04:49.664 --> 04:52.000
<i>It will be like killing two birds</i>
<i>with one stone.</i>

04:52.083 --> 04:54.669
I see!
I couldn't expect less from you, Chrome!

04:54.752 --> 04:58.131
And who's going to light the bomb fuse?

04:58.214 --> 05:00.883
Dr. Xeno is surely
not going to do it himself.

05:08.057 --> 05:10.351
-It's going to explode!
-Got it!

05:13.813 --> 05:15.481
Hurry up, everyone!

05:30.204 --> 05:32.749
<i>Did we make it…?</i>

05:33.499 --> 05:34.917
Looks like they collapsed.

05:35.752 --> 05:37.420
Both sides did.

05:37.503 --> 05:38.671
-What?
-What?

05:39.338 --> 05:40.173
Damn!

05:41.591 --> 05:43.551
Let's quickly circle around
from the ground

05:43.634 --> 05:47.013
and find the tunnel exit.
If we capture it now…

05:49.515 --> 05:52.101
Relax, kiddo!

05:52.185 --> 05:55.063
No matter what,
that's going to lead to a battle.

05:55.688 --> 05:57.815
While we're wasting time like this,

05:57.899 --> 06:00.068
all the ones buried will probably die.

06:01.152 --> 06:02.945
There's no one in this world

06:03.988 --> 06:06.532
who deserves to die!

06:06.616 --> 06:07.450
That's why…

06:08.367 --> 06:10.536
we'll dig from both sides!

06:12.246 --> 06:15.041
It’s a speed contest to see

06:15.708 --> 06:18.002
who can dig the fastest!

06:26.052 --> 06:28.262
Chrome, are you by any chance

06:28.346 --> 06:30.556
a descendant of the surviving humans?

06:31.766 --> 06:33.226
How did it go?

06:33.810 --> 06:36.020
A plan to escape by building a tunnel

06:36.104 --> 06:38.940
and a monorail in this Stone World.

06:39.023 --> 06:43.069
Ah, it's truly truly elegant!

06:43.152 --> 06:46.405
But, Chrome,
use that intelligence of yours

06:46.489 --> 06:48.366
and think rationally.

06:48.866 --> 06:50.576
In which direction should you dig?

06:50.660 --> 06:53.079
In which direction should you go?

06:53.830 --> 06:56.874
Your ship and friends have
already been destroyed.

06:57.458 --> 06:59.460
Stan has seized them all.

07:01.254 --> 07:03.297
<i>The matter is settled.</i>

07:04.048 --> 07:05.925
<i>I'm not planning to kill anyone else.</i>

07:06.425 --> 07:09.011
<i>You only need to be</i>

07:09.095 --> 07:12.765
<i>a part of this new Earth, the one I rule.</i>

07:15.518 --> 07:18.187
And what makes you the one in charge?

07:18.688 --> 07:20.940
I shall lead the people.

07:22.483 --> 07:24.277
Even in the 21st century…

07:24.861 --> 07:26.904
<i>All those fools who rambled on</i>

07:26.988 --> 07:29.907
<i>about ethics, politics, and other nonsense</i>

07:29.991 --> 07:32.660
<i>only held back the progress of mankind.</i>

07:33.494 --> 07:35.663
<i>I bet you had them around you too.</i>

07:35.746 --> 07:37.957
<i>People who couldn't understand</i>
<i>the value of science</i>

07:38.040 --> 07:41.043
<i>and only knew how to swing their fists.</i>

07:41.127 --> 07:45.006
Well, I guess so…

07:46.048 --> 07:47.425
Chrome…

07:47.508 --> 07:50.428
You like science, don't you?

07:50.511 --> 07:52.138
And you believe in science, don't you?

07:52.805 --> 07:57.268
Yes, I’m an unstoppable force of science.

07:57.852 --> 07:59.854
You could become a leader

07:59.937 --> 08:03.733
and use the power of science
to rule over the fools!

08:05.026 --> 08:06.736
Sure.

08:06.819 --> 08:09.989
I just can't understand
musclebrains like Magma

08:10.072 --> 08:11.657
who are so obsessed with muscles

08:11.741 --> 08:13.910
and value them more than anything else.

08:15.411 --> 08:16.662
But still…

08:17.413 --> 08:19.582
Whether I understand or not,

08:19.665 --> 08:21.501
and whether they're fools or not,

08:21.584 --> 08:25.171
It’s not my place to look down on others
based on what they like.

08:39.685 --> 08:41.979
It's all secured, Senku!

08:43.564 --> 08:47.568
<i>The enemy ruler, Dr. Xeno!</i>

08:54.659 --> 08:58.079
<i>Senku… And the others on the plane…</i>

09:00.039 --> 09:02.333
You're impressive, Stanley!

09:02.416 --> 09:05.711
You took the enemy's main base
in less than a minute!

09:05.795 --> 09:07.672
Oh, Max!

09:08.548 --> 09:10.716
My lady! Thank goodness you're safe!

09:10.800 --> 09:13.177
But what is this? Why are you like this?

09:13.261 --> 09:15.221
Mumble, mumble…

09:15.304 --> 09:16.597
I finally got a boyfriend.

09:23.563 --> 09:25.231
His plane was shot down, right?

09:25.314 --> 09:28.192
Who do you need
to join that boyfriend's rescue team?

09:28.276 --> 09:30.027
I can ask Francois to help

09:30.111 --> 09:31.362
with first aid…

09:31.445 --> 09:34.574
The rescue might require
dismantling the aircraft.

09:34.657 --> 09:36.325
You should ask Kaseki.

09:38.619 --> 09:39.829
It's fine.

09:39.912 --> 09:42.123
I can cut the rope myself.

09:43.249 --> 09:47.461
Please, tell me about some interesting
crafting items that Xeno has.

09:47.545 --> 09:51.090
A blade spins with the help of an engine,
and the fields are plowed automatically.

09:51.173 --> 09:52.675
It's called a tractor.

09:57.847 --> 10:00.224
Two of them fell into the river!

10:00.308 --> 10:02.518
We'll go save them!

10:09.650 --> 10:10.735
Right now, we're hiding

10:10.818 --> 10:13.904
on the riverbank to the west-northwest
of the enemy’s main base.

10:13.988 --> 10:15.865
Since we've captured Xeno,

10:15.948 --> 10:18.409
Japanese now sounds
like an encrypted code,

10:18.492 --> 10:21.412
as there's no one else among them
who understands it.

10:21.495 --> 10:24.957
Yes, there's no need
to tie him up so tightly.

10:30.588 --> 10:32.882
We can't even search properly

10:32.965 --> 10:35.509
until Stanley and the others return,

10:35.593 --> 10:39.180
so I'm not stupid enough
to cause a meaningless disturbance.

10:42.016 --> 10:45.102
This man, Dr. Xeno,

10:45.686 --> 10:48.731
is a top scientist in the world.

11:01.160 --> 11:04.955
Oh, so you're alive, Dr. Senku.

11:05.581 --> 11:08.417
There's no way Stanley missed his target.

11:08.918 --> 11:10.211
So, Senku,

11:10.294 --> 11:13.464
this means you managed to survive

11:13.547 --> 11:15.883
by using science to defeat bullets.

11:17.551 --> 11:20.763
Science is truly elegant!

11:22.473 --> 11:25.309
It's been a few thousand years
since I was a third grader

11:25.393 --> 11:26.811
sending emails to NASA.

11:28.604 --> 11:30.773
If you want to talk about fun memories,

11:30.856 --> 11:33.067
we've got plenty of time ahead.

11:33.150 --> 11:35.528
We're not moving until the sun goes down.

11:36.112 --> 11:37.488
Ahead?

11:37.571 --> 11:39.532
Where are you planning to go?

11:39.615 --> 11:41.200
You've nowhere to go back to.

11:41.283 --> 11:45.037
We've seized your ship
and all of your friends.

11:45.788 --> 11:47.206
The battle is over.

11:49.458 --> 11:51.877
Exactly! We've got nowhere to go back to.

11:51.961 --> 11:54.880
So we just move forward, right?

11:55.381 --> 11:56.757
What do you mean?

11:59.218 --> 12:03.472
Look! It's the place
that was sent through the phone.

12:07.560 --> 12:09.728
You're all right, Senku!

12:11.439 --> 12:12.982
But I already knew that!

12:13.065 --> 12:14.567
I'm cool,

12:14.650 --> 12:17.319
and you're not the type to fall so easily.

12:22.241 --> 12:24.535
You just arrived,
and you're already hosting.

12:25.119 --> 12:27.496
My lady! I'm glad you're safe!

12:27.580 --> 12:29.540
You too, Carlos…

12:35.838 --> 12:37.298
I wanted to see you.

12:37.381 --> 12:39.425
Did you escape just so you could see me?

12:39.508 --> 12:41.760
You're amazing, Luna.

12:41.844 --> 12:44.847
Please, stop. It's not like that.

12:51.270 --> 12:52.646
Taking advantage of the confusion,

12:52.730 --> 12:56.400
you took Kaseki and Francois
and escaped with them?

12:56.484 --> 12:58.277
You're amazing, Luna.

13:01.655 --> 13:03.115
I was half right.

13:04.366 --> 13:08.162
But we're the only ones left
to keep going.

13:08.245 --> 13:11.165
The only ones…

13:13.083 --> 13:18.130
If Stanley's or Maya's main force returns
from their expedition, it's all over.

13:18.214 --> 13:21.342
Then now's our chance
while their resources are low.

13:21.425 --> 13:23.177
They wouldn’t expect us to return

13:23.260 --> 13:26.514
right after we just escaped.

13:39.109 --> 13:42.947
I'm borrowing your boat for a while, Xeno!

13:43.030 --> 13:45.533
Consider it a trade for the Perseus!

13:51.080 --> 13:53.791
I wonder if Stanley
would attack this boat.

13:53.874 --> 13:57.127
You're always
thinking about fighting, Kohaku.

13:57.211 --> 13:59.880
If that happened, we'd wipe them out.

14:00.923 --> 14:02.258
Our objective…

14:03.050 --> 14:04.426
is diplomacy.

14:04.510 --> 14:10.015
Let's have the first and last
Japan-US summit in the New World.

14:10.599 --> 14:11.809
As for the enemies,

14:11.892 --> 14:15.104
who should we talk to
on the American team?

14:17.314 --> 14:20.109
I have a feeling about a certain one.

14:21.694 --> 14:23.028
<i>A guy who refused to fight</i>

14:23.112 --> 14:26.740
<i>and tried to dig a hole</i>
<i>to save us instead.</i>

14:28.242 --> 14:31.620
I believe you're referring to Brody,
the mechanic.

14:31.704 --> 14:34.039
That time he caught me lying,

14:34.748 --> 14:38.168
<i>he just laughed it off</i>
<i>instead of getting angry.</i>

14:38.252 --> 14:42.798
<i>He's just like Ukyo,</i>
<i>avoiding unnecessary sacrifices.</i>

14:48.846 --> 14:51.015
Hi! Were you asking for me?

14:51.098 --> 14:53.017
If you're looking for a hostage exchange,

14:53.100 --> 14:55.936
there's a huge difference
in numbers, kiddo.

14:56.020 --> 14:58.355
Yes, you're right.

14:58.439 --> 15:01.066
So, to fill that gap,
I'll give you some information

15:01.150 --> 15:04.820
that I'm ten billion percent sure
will be too tempting for you to resist.

15:06.113 --> 15:07.114
What do you…

15:07.698 --> 15:09.617
The recipe for
the Petrification Revival Fluid

15:09.700 --> 15:12.661
is Nital,
a mixture of alcohol and nitric acid.

15:17.541 --> 15:20.502
<i>In other words, you can make</i>
<i>as much as you want from corn.</i>

15:20.586 --> 15:23.130
<i>Since my friends on the ship</i>
<i>know how to make it,</i>

15:23.213 --> 15:26.967
<i>let's all get along and cooperate.</i>

15:27.051 --> 15:31.847
I'm going to wake one million people
who turned into stone!

15:33.432 --> 15:35.809
But Senku, a million…

15:37.061 --> 15:38.979
If we're planning to go to the moon,

15:39.063 --> 15:42.232
we need unlimited manpower, don't we?

15:42.816 --> 15:46.779
<i>Our only purpose for coming here,</i>
<i>to America,</i>

15:46.862 --> 15:49.573
<i>was building a huge city of corn.</i>

15:49.657 --> 15:52.910
<i>It doesn't sound bad to you either, right?</i>

15:54.119 --> 15:55.496
What about Xeno?

15:55.579 --> 16:00.876
We'll keep him safe
as long as you don't betray us.

16:01.585 --> 16:04.171
Building a city of one million people…

16:04.254 --> 16:06.131
No, that's more like a country.

16:06.882 --> 16:08.467
I guess joining forces

16:09.009 --> 16:12.388
after taking each other’s hostages
is out of the question.

16:12.471 --> 16:14.264
I guess so…

16:14.348 --> 16:17.643
<i>Even if we agreed,</i>

16:18.352 --> 16:20.604
I'm not sure Stanley will be happy.

16:21.230 --> 16:25.275
He'll chase Xeno and you
to the ends of the Earth.

16:25.359 --> 16:28.821
<i>In that case,</i>
<i>we'll dodge him to the ends of hell.</i>

16:28.904 --> 16:30.614
<i>We're kind of busy here.</i>

16:30.698 --> 16:33.117
<i>We'll push ahead full throttle.</i>

16:34.702 --> 16:37.162
You really are out of your mind!

16:37.830 --> 16:40.499
<i>That's all. I'll leave the rest to you.</i>

16:41.500 --> 16:45.796
<i>Yes, leave it to us.</i>

16:49.550 --> 16:52.928
<i>We'll blow this Stone World up!</i>

16:53.012 --> 16:55.806
<i>For the million-person corn city!</i>

16:57.391 --> 17:00.519
This means this will be the place
where we say goodbye

17:00.602 --> 17:02.730
to everyone who will build the corn city.

17:05.024 --> 17:07.568
<i>Yuzuriha… Everyone…</i>

17:08.277 --> 17:11.697
We've got to keep on moving right away.

17:11.780 --> 17:13.657
Be sure to hold a Japan-US summit

17:13.741 --> 17:16.326
with those who will
actually build the city.

17:18.037 --> 17:20.289
Hey, what does that mean?

17:20.372 --> 17:22.207
Was he talking to us?

17:22.291 --> 17:25.252
They can't really
understand each other, right?

17:25.335 --> 17:26.962
Is there someone who speaks English?

17:27.046 --> 17:29.715
I’m technically a reporter, so…

17:29.798 --> 17:31.216
But it's just broken English.

17:31.300 --> 17:33.844
You just remember the lyrics
to Lillian's song, right?

17:40.726 --> 17:44.855
Our first request
the safety of everyone here.

17:44.938 --> 17:47.566
Hi there, President of Japan.

17:47.649 --> 17:50.444
Don't get the wrong idea.
The initiative is ours.

17:50.527 --> 17:51.945
<i>This is about military power.</i>

17:52.029 --> 17:54.448
Shut it up already!

17:54.531 --> 17:56.700
Hurry up and untie me!

17:56.784 --> 17:59.078
Not just me! Everyone!

17:59.661 --> 18:01.830
We'll get to that in a moment.

18:01.914 --> 18:04.541
But first, the Revival Fluid…

18:04.625 --> 18:06.335
N-O-W!

18:06.418 --> 18:09.797
How many corn kernels are in you ears,
senile old man?

18:09.880 --> 18:13.133
After coming this far,
we're not negotiating a damn thing!

18:13.801 --> 18:15.427
<i>Even if we're on different sides,</i>

18:15.511 --> 18:19.598
<i>we're going to build the</i>
<i>one million-person corn city together.</i>

18:19.681 --> 18:21.975
If you extend your right hand
for a handshake,

18:22.059 --> 18:24.520
we'll firmly extend our right hand too!

18:24.603 --> 18:26.188
It's a gentlemen's agreement.

18:26.271 --> 18:28.357
It's our only option now!

18:31.735 --> 18:34.571
Okay, sounds fine. I like this.

18:34.655 --> 18:36.698
You've got a strong personality, girl.

18:36.782 --> 18:38.826
As interim presidents,

18:38.909 --> 18:41.411
let's work together
and sign the agreement.

18:42.079 --> 18:46.416
<i>Until we get Dr. Xeno back, this corn city</i>

18:46.500 --> 18:49.920
<i>will be the special peace zone</i>
<i>for the revived million people</i>

18:53.423 --> 18:56.343
We've got a deal, kiddo.

18:56.426 --> 18:58.053
Senku, wasn't it?

18:58.137 --> 18:59.721
The rest is up to Xeno.

18:59.805 --> 19:02.391
He’ll just have to desperately escape
with all he's got.

19:03.225 --> 19:06.770
<i>Stanley is the only one no one can stop.</i>

19:08.313 --> 19:10.190
Senku…

19:10.274 --> 19:12.317
Why are you still alive?

19:13.986 --> 19:15.571
They're coming from upstream!

19:35.716 --> 19:38.343
Isn't that Medusa on the front?

19:40.470 --> 19:41.638
Whisper, whisper…

19:42.598 --> 19:44.349
It's the petrification beam!

19:46.685 --> 19:48.353
This is bad!

20:06.330 --> 20:08.457
I see…

20:09.041 --> 20:11.335
<i>There's no petrification device.</i>

20:11.418 --> 20:13.337
<i>Or maybe it doesn't work.</i>

20:14.129 --> 20:17.591
<i>It was all made up by Gen. Just a bluff…</i>

20:18.967 --> 20:20.594
I don't like that…

20:21.470 --> 20:23.472
-They passed through.
-To the sea.

20:26.141 --> 20:27.309
Damn…

20:32.940 --> 20:35.150
-We're parting ways!
-Wait!

20:36.193 --> 20:41.448
Going onto the deck now to say goodbye
might turn into a beehive situation.

20:41.531 --> 20:45.369
Knowing the risks, what's more important?

20:51.166 --> 20:52.376
About that…

20:55.337 --> 20:56.630
I'll take the risk!

20:57.464 --> 21:01.218
Hey!

21:01.802 --> 21:06.431
Hey!

21:07.140 --> 21:10.852
Hey!

21:11.728 --> 21:16.191
Hey!

21:17.192 --> 21:21.488
Hey!

21:33.875 --> 21:34.918
We'll meet again…

21:35.502 --> 21:36.920
Everyone!

21:37.963 --> 21:40.215
Build cities all around the world!

21:43.135 --> 21:44.761
From here,

21:44.845 --> 21:47.306
we'll be playing tag full-on
with Stanley's crew

21:47.389 --> 21:49.641
while circling the Earth.

21:51.601 --> 21:54.980
Exactly! And our next destination is…

21:55.564 --> 21:57.858
<i>Yes, South America.</i>

21:57.941 --> 22:00.277
<i>Let's go. To the place of origin</i>

22:00.360 --> 22:03.113
<i>of the beam that turned</i>
<i>almost all of humanity into stone,</i>

22:03.196 --> 22:04.906
<i>a few thousand years ago!</i>

22:11.246 --> 22:14.374
<i>This is tempting…</i>

23:53.348 --> 23:55.976
NEXT EPISODE

23:56.059 --> 23:58.436
THIS WORK OF FICTION FEATURES ORGANISMS,
MATERIAL AND PROCESSES BASED ON REAL LIFE.

23:58.520 --> 24:00.981
COLLECTING OR REPLICATING THEM MAY BE
DANGEROUS AND ILLEGAL, SO DO NOT ATTEMPT.

24:01.064 --> 24:01.940
Subtitle translation by: Silvia
